  levelId: level_24
  levelTitle: Opposite Directions - Diode Challenge
  initialPage: 0
  pages:
  - title: LEVEL 24 | Opposite Directions | Circuit Overview
    explanation: 'ILLUSTRATIVE / NOT LIVE VERIFIED. One 5 V supply and switch feed
      R1 330 Ohm, then split into two parallel branches. The upper branch is D1 forward:
      anode at the resistor side, banded cathode toward the green LED. The lower
      branch is D2 reverse: banded cathode at the resistor side, anode toward the
      LED. Both paths join before the LED. The LED cathode returns to Battery_negative.
      D1 conducts; D2 blocks. Never bypass the resistor, LED, or both diodes with
      a direct wire.'
    caption: PAGE 1/4 | 5 V | SWITCH | 330 OHM | 2 OPPOSING DIODES | GREEN LED
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.09, y: 0.52}
      label: 5 V
      color: {r: 0.98, g: 0.29, b: 0.35, a: 1}
    - id: sw1
      kind: 5
      position: {x: 0.26, y: 0.78}
      label: SW1
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.78, b: 0.28, a: 1}
    - id: r1
      kind: 1
      position: {x: 0.44, y: 0.78}
      label: R1 330 Ohm
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.78, b: 0.28, a: 1}
    - id: d1
      kind: 3
      position: {x: 0.67, y: 0.78}
      label: D1 FORWARD  A >| K
      color: {r: 0.28, g: 0.93, b: 0.98, a: 1}
    - id: d2
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.67, y: 0.54}
      label: D2 REVERSE  K |< A
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.62, b: 0.25, a: 1}
    - id: led1
      kind: 2
      position: {x: 0.9, y: 0.78}
      label: LED1 GREEN  A >| K
      color: {r: 0.3, g: 0.98, b: 0.59, a: 1}
    - id: gnd
      kind: 6
      position: {x: 0.55, y: 0.17}
      label: BATTERY NEGATIVE / GND
      color: {r: 0.19, g: 0.74, b: 1, a: 1}
