  - title: LEVEL 24 | Exact Seven Electrical Connections
    explanation: 'CONNECT SEVEN WIRES: (1) Battery_positive -> SwitchInput. (2) SwitchOutput
      -> R_LIMIT_Input. (3) R_LIMIT_Output -> D_FORWARD_Anode. (4) R_LIMIT_Output
      -> D_REVERSE_Cathode. (5) D_FORWARD_Cathode -> LED_Anode. (6) D_REVERSE_Anode
      -> LED_Anode. (7) LED_Cathode -> Battery_negative. Runtime binding IDs identify
      the physical SparkTerminals. The circuit requires multiple connections at the
      branch terminals, or explicit junctions supported by the wire system. If the
      first battery-to-switch wire is preinstalled, the player adds six.'
    caption: PAGE 2/4 | TWO BRANCHES | SHARED START + SHARED END
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
