  - title: LEVEL 24 | Forward Conducts, Reverse Blocks
    explanation: 'The two diode branches are in parallel between the same pair of
      nodes. D1 points from resistor toward LED: forward bias, approximately +0.7
      V from D_FORWARD_Anode to D_FORWARD_Cathode, and positive branch current. D2
      points the opposite way: D_REVERSE_Cathode at the high-potential side, D_REVERSE_Anode
      at the low-potential side, approximately -0.7 V signed anode-to-cathode voltage
      and near-zero reverse current. The reverse Generic schematic symbol is deliberately
      labeled K |< A rather than drawing a possibly forward-facing built-in diode
      icon.'
    caption: PAGE 3/4 | D1 A >| K | D2 K |< A
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.09, y: 0.52}
      label: 5 V
